{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to share a release-impacting finding from backend engineering. While testing an unrelated bulk-import client yesterday, I measured legitimate synchronization bursts of 145 requests in a minute. Our load replay confirms the policy needs an ordinary API-key limit of exactly 150 requests per minute with a 60-second burst window. I hadn't updated the draft because the client test was owned by another team, but this is critical for the review."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "I have a release-impacting finding from customer success. I confirmed with Acme's account team this morning that Acme's contract requires 14 calendar days' notice before enforcing a new API limit on Acme traffic. A notice sent on September 1 would permit enforcement on exactly September 15. I haven't entered the clause in the product launch ticket yet because legal confirmation arrived after the weekly review, but this contractual notice requirement needs to be factored into our launch timing and customer communications."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "I have a release-impacting finding from security. During a credential-abuse investigation this afternoon, I measured automated login attempts against the authentication endpoints and confirmed that those endpoints require a separate limit of exactly 30 requests per minute per API key. This is lower than the 100 requests per minute currently in the draft, and applying the same 100 RPM limit to auth endpoints would leave them vulnerable to credential-stuffing attacks. The finding isn't in the security tracker yet because the investigation is still being closed, but this needs to be reflected in the final policy before it goes to customers."}
```

